      "content": "the thing is, i've already reached out to management and they just brushed it off like it's nothing. they keep saying it's \"standard operational noise\" but it's not just a noise, it feels intentional. like the rhythm of the hum changes when i'm in the room. have you ever heard of buildings using infrasound or specific low-frequency modulations for things like mood regulation or behavioral control? i'm starting to think it's not just a mechanical glitch.",
