      "content": "i tried documenting it but it's harder than it looks because the \"noise\" isn't something you can just record on a phone, it's too low actually. it's more of a physical sensation. i was reading some stuff online about how certain infrasonic frequencies can actually induce anxiety or a sense of being watched, and i'm starting to get really paranoid that this isn't just a glitch. if it was a mechanical issue, it would be random, but this feels... synchronized. like a pattern. what kind of materials or shielding would actually block these kinds of low-frequency waves? i feel like i need to do something to protect my space.",
